---
const ingredients = [
{ name: 'Shea butter', note: 'supports the barrier', flag: false },
{ name: 'Glycerin', note: 'draws in moisture', flag: false },
{ name: 'Alcohol denat.', note: 'may dry your skin', flag: true },
];
---

<section class="sec ruled" id="labels">
<div class="wrap">
<div class="story reveal">
<div>
<span class="kicker kicker--accent">Product analysis</span>
<h2 class="display">Point at any label. Know in seconds.</h2>
</div>
<p class="story__statement">
We read the ingredients you sent us and say what each one does for your skin —
or against it. No verdict without the ingredient that caused it.
</p>
</div>

<div class="split">
<div class="stage reveal">
<img
src="/images/cream-jar.webp"
width="900"
height="900"
alt="A plain frosted cream jar on a pale ceramic plate in afternoon light."
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
/>
<span class="tagchip tagchip--a"><i></i> No fragrance</span>
<span class="tagchip tagchip--b"><i></i> Barrier support</span>
</div>

<div class="reveal">
<ul class="ingredients">
{
ingredients.map((i) => (
<li class={i.flag ? 'flag' : ''}>
<b>{i.name}</b>
<span>{i.note}</span>
</li>
))
}
</ul>

<div class="match match--float">
<div class="match__top">
<div class="match__thumb" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<div>
<div class="match__name">Fragrance-free barrier cream</div>
<div class="match__meta">Good match · 0.82 confidence</div>
</div>
</div>
<p class="match__reason">
<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
<path
d="m3 8.5 3 3 7-7"
stroke="currentColor"
stroke-width="1.8"
stroke-linecap="round"
stroke-linejoin="round"
/>
</svg>
Ceramides and glycerin, no fragrance — that suits the dryness and texture
the scan found.
</p>
</div>

<p class="demo__note">
We only flag an ingredient when we have read enough of the label. Below 60% of
ingredients matched, we ask for a clearer photo instead of guessing.
</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
